{title: Colors of The Wind}
{artist: Alan Menken}
{lyricist: Stephen Schwartz}
{year: 1995}
{meta: firstline You think you own whatever land you land on}
{meta: movie Pocahontas}
{define: "First note" copy "g"}

[<hidden>First note</hidden>]
{comment: Verse 1}
You [C]think you own whatever land you [Am]land on
the [C]earth is just a dead thing can [Em]claim
but [Am]I know every rock and tree and [F]creature
has a [Dm]life, has a [G]spirit, has a [Am]name. 


{comment: Verse 2}
You [C]think the only people who are [Am]people
are the [C]people who look and think like [Em]you
but [Am]if you walk the footsteps of a [F]stranger
you'll learn [Dm]things you never [G7]knew you never [C]knew.
 

{start_of_chorus}
 Have you [Am]ever heard the wolf cry to the [Em]blue corn [F]moon
Or [Am]asked the grinning bobcat why he [Em]grinned?
Can you [F]sing with all the voices of the [C]mountain?
Can you [Dm]paint with all the [G]colors of the [Am]wind?
Can you [F]paint with all the [G7]colors of the [C]wind?
{end_of_chorus} 


{comment: Verse 3}
Come [C]run the hidden pine trails of the [Am]forest
Come [C]taste the sunsweet berries of the [Em]earth
Come [Am]roll in all the riches all a[F]round you
And for [Dm]once never [G]wonder what they're [Am]worth.


{comment: Verse 4}
The [C]rainstorm and the river are my [Am]brothers
The [C]heron and the otter are my [Em]friends
And [Am]we are all connected to each [F]other
In a [Dm]circle in a [G7]hoop that never [C]ends.
 

{comment: Bridge} 
[C]How [F]high does the [Em]sycamore [Am]grow?
If you [F]cut it down then you'll [G]never know.


{comment: Outro}
{start_of_chorus}
And you'll [Am]never hear the wolf cry to the [Em]blue corn [F]moon
For [Am]whether we are white or copper [Em]skinned,
We need to [F]sing with all the voices of the [C]mountain, [Am]
We need to [F]paint with all the colors of the [Am]wind.

You can [F]own the Earth and [G]still
All you'll [Em]own is earth un[F]til
You can [Am]paint with all the [F]colors [G7]of the [C]wind.
{end_of_chorus}
